            {'name': 'Diffblue Testing Agent', 'tagline': 'AI agent that writes verified Java and Python unit tests, billed per line of coverage added', 'desc': "Diffblue Testing Agent uses reinforcement learning to autonomously generate unit tests across entire codebases, with every test guaranteed to compile, pass, and add real coverage before you're billed for it.", 'pricing': 'Outcome-based: standard package starts at $1,500 for 5,000 net-new lines of verified coverage (about $0.30/line); larger packages and Enterprise (volume pricing, SSO/SAML, on-prem, SLA) are custom. Free trial offered but terms not stated. Community and Developer editions could not be verified on the live pricing page.', 'url': 'https://www.diffblue.com/', 'tags': ['Coding & Development', 'Unit Testing', 'AI Agent', 'Test Automation'], 'features': ['Autonomous batch test generation across a repository', 'Every counted test compiles, passes and adds coverage', 'Task mode in the IDE plus batch mode for projects', 'Java 8, 11, 17, 21, 25 and Python 3.9+', 'Works with GitHub Copilot CLI and Claude Code', 'Diffblue Cover: offline, deterministic Java test generation for air-gapped use'], 'pros': ['You pay for verified net-new coverage, not for broken or flaky tests', 'Batch mode can cover whole repositories without per-file prompting', 'Works alongside GitHub Copilot CLI and Claude Code', 'Coverage billed is checkable with JaCoCo or Cobertura'], 'cons': ['Supports Java and Python only', 'Starts at $1,500, which is steep for small teams or hobby projects', 'Unit tests only; does not replace integration or end-to-end testing', 'Larger package prices are not published'], 'best_for': 'Enterprise Java teams (and Python teams) in regulated industries that need to raise unit test coverage fast on large legacy codebases before refactoring or modernizing.', 'deep': {'overview': 'Diffblue Testing Agent is a strong choice for large enterprise teams with big, under-tested Java codebases who need coverage fast and want to pay only for results. Skip it if you work in other languages, have a small project, or want a cheap per-seat assistant, since the entry package is $1,500. It is an AI agent that generates, verifies and fixes unit tests across a codebase, either in batch mode for whole projects or in task mode inside an IDE. Each test is checked to compile, pass and add coverage before it counts, and billing follows the net-new coverage lines it adds. It can work with GitHub Copilot and Claude Code, and the separate Diffblue Cover product offers offline, deterministic Java generation without an LLM for air-gapped environments.', 'features_detailed': [{'title': 'Batch mode', 'desc': 'Generates tests across an entire repository in one run instead of file-by-file prompting.'}, {'title': 'Task mode in the IDE', 'desc': 'Generate and fix tests for specific code from within your development environment.'}, {'title': 'Built-in verification', 'desc': 'Tests must compile, pass and increase coverage to count; failing or flaky ones are discarded and not billed.'}, {'title': 'Works with AI coding tools', 'desc': 'Integrates with GitHub Copilot CLI and Claude Code; Gemini CLI and Codex are listed as coming soon.'}, {'title': 'Language support', 'desc': 'Java 8, 11, 17, 21 and 25, plus Python 3.9 and above.'}, {'title': 'Diffblue Cover', 'desc': 'A separate offline, deterministic Java test generator with no LLM dependency, aimed at air-gapped environments.'}], 'pricing_plans': [{'name': 'Standard package', 'price': 'Starting at $1,500 for 5,000 net-new lines (about $0.30/line)', 'billing': 'Pay once for verified coverage added, measured against baseline coverage', 'features': ['Unit tests for classes and methods', 'Batch mode for entire repositories', 'Works with GitHub Copilot CLI and Claude Code', 'Built-in verification', 'Java and Python']}, {'name': 'Larger packages / Enterprise', 'price': 'Custom, not published', 'billing': 'Contact sales', 'features': ['Volume pricing', 'SSO/SAML', 'Dedicated support and SLA', 'On-premises deployment', 'Multi-repository support']}, {'name': 'Free trial', 'price': 'Not stated', 'billing': 'Trial link exists; length and limits not stated on the pricing page', 'features': ['Terms unverified']}], 'pros_expanded': ['Billing tied to net-new verified coverage means you do not pay for tests that fail, are flaky or add nothing, and you can audit the number with JaCoCo or Cobertura.', 'Batch mode is built for project-scale work, which is where per-prompt assistants become tedious on legacy code.', 'Verification happens before tests are counted, so reviewers should see fewer broken tests to clean up.', 'Can run alongside Copilot CLI and Claude Code instead of replacing them.', 'Diffblue Cover covers offline, no-LLM use for air-gapped or regulated environments.'], 'cons_expanded': ['Only Java and Python are supported, so polyglot teams still need another tool for other languages.', "The $1,500 minimum for 5,000 lines is a real commitment before you know how much coverage your code gains; the free trial's terms are not stated on the pricing page.", 'Pricing for larger packages and Enterprise is not public.', 'It targets unit tests only, so integration and end-to-end gaps remain.', 'Coverage lines are a quantity metric; high coverage does not guarantee tests assert meaningful behavior, so some human review is still wise.', 'I could not confirm today whether a free Community Edition or a per-developer Developer Edition still exist; they appear only in older material.'], 'who_for': 'Good for enterprise engineering orgs with large Java (or Python) codebases, especially in banking, insurance, defense or healthcare, who need coverage uplift before modernization. Not for small teams or hobby projects, non-Java/Python stacks, or anyone wanting integration or end-to-end test generation.', 'faq': [{'q': 'How does Diffblue charge?', 'a': 'By net-new lines of verified coverage. Baseline coverage is measured first, then you pay for the difference. The standard package starts at $1,500 for 5,000 lines (about $0.30/line).'}, {'q': 'Which languages are supported?', 'a': 'Java 8, 11, 17, 21 and 25, and Python 3.9 and above.'}, {'q': 'Does it replace Copilot or Claude Code?', 'a': 'No. It works alongside GitHub Copilot CLI and Claude Code, and adds batch generation plus verification.'}, {'q': 'Can it run offline?', 'a': 'Diffblue Cover, the separate product, generates Java tests offline and deterministically without an LLM, aimed at air-gapped environments.'}, {'q': 'Is there a free option?', 'a': 'A free trial link exists, but the pricing page does not state its length or limits. A Community Edition was listed previously but could not be verified today.'}]}, 'alternatives': [{'slug': 'github-copilot', 'why': 'Pick Copilot for cheap, prompt-driven test drafting across many languages, at the cost of manual review per test.'}, {'slug': 'claude-code', 'why': 'Pick Claude Code for agentic, language-flexible test writing in your own repo where you review output yourself.'}], 'last_checked': '2026-10-27'},
            
